IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ba-house`

-- Building Act 2011 (WA), the home owner building a house -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_building-act-2011_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe/facts.json and SCENARIO.md: c055 (2029-07-15)
-- Chloe (26) and Liam take handover of their new house in Byford, built under a house-and-land package signed in
-- February 2028 with a builder under the Home Building Contracts Act and with indemnity insurance; the land settled in May
-- 2028 on a Torrens title. That Chloe is a registered proprietor, that the builder was named on a building permit granted
-- on a certified application with an independent surveyor's certificate, and whether the Building Regulations 2012 exempt
-- the house from s 41, are ASSUMED for the cases; the scenario does not say, and the regulations are not deposited.
-- Variants change one fact each.

§ `fixtures`

`Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` MEANS Person WITH
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS TRUE
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS FALSE
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS FALSE

`the builder named on Chloe's permit` MEANS Person WITH
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS FALSE
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS FALSE
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS TRUE

`a tenant renting the house` MEANS Person WITH
    `is registered as a proprietor of the land` IS FALSE
    `holds a prescribed interest in the land` IS FALSE
    `is named as the builder on the building permit` IS FALSE

`c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit` MEANS Work WITH
    `kind` IS `building a new house or other building`
    `the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit` IS FALSE
    `is to remain erected for no longer than one month` IS FALSE
    `members of the public will use it or be permitted access` IS FALSE
    `is done in accordance with a building order` IS FALSE
    `a building permit is in effect for it` IS TRUE

`the Byford house built with no permit` MEANS Work WITH
    `kind` IS `building a new house or other building`
    `the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit` IS FALSE
    `is to remain erected for no longer than one month` IS FALSE
    `members of the public will use it or be permitted access` IS FALSE
    `is done in accordance with a building order` IS FALSE
    `a building permit is in effect for it` IS FALSE

`a garden shed the regulations exempt` MEANS Work WITH
    `kind` IS `building a swimming pool, fence, retaining wall or other incidental structure`
    `the regulations or a Ministerial order say it needs no building permit` IS TRUE
    `is to remain erected for no longer than one month` IS FALSE
    `members of the public will use it or be permitted access` IS FALSE
    `is done in accordance with a building order` IS FALSE
    `a building permit is in effect for it` IS FALSE

