§ `s 3 -- building work`

-- c055: building the house is building work (s 3 para (a)).
#ASSERT `Is it building work` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit`
-- Demolition is demolition work, defined separately.
#ASSERT NOT `Is it building work` `demolishing the old house`

§ `s 9, s 69 -- do I need a building permit`

-- c055: the new house needed a building permit.
#ASSERT `Do I need a building permit` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit`
#ASSERT NOT `Do I need a building permit` `a garden shed the regulations exempt`
-- s 69(1): up for no longer than one month.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I need a building permit` `a site office up for three weeks, closed to the public`
-- s 69(2): the exemption is lost if the public use it.
#ASSERT `Do I need a building permit` `a display home up for three weeks, open to the public`
-- s 9(c).
#ASSERT NOT `Do I need a building permit` `rectification work under a building order`

§ `s 9, ss 11, 12 -- building without a permit`

#ASSERT `Would doing the work be an offence` `the Byford house built with no permit` FALSE FALSE
-- c055: a permit was in effect.
#ASSERT NOT `Would doing the work be an offence` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit` FALSE FALSE
-- s 11: the permit was suspended without the owner's knowing.
#ASSERT NOT `Would doing the work be an offence` `the Byford house built with no permit` TRUE FALSE
-- First offence.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` 0 EQUALS 50000
-- Second offence.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` 1 EQUALS 75000
-- Fourth offence: third or subsequent.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` 3 EQUALS 100000
-- Third offence.
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` 2 EQUALS 12
-- No imprisonment for a first offence.
#ASSERT `What is the longest I can be imprisoned in months` 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 5, s 16 -- the owner, and who signs`

-- c055: Chloe, a registered proprietor, is an owner (s 5(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `Am I an owner` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an owner` `a tenant renting the house`
-- s 16(c): the builder signs too.
#ASSERT `Must I sign the building permit application` `the builder named on Chloe's permit`
#ASSERT NOT `Must I sign the building permit application` `a tenant renting the house`

§ `ss 16, 17 -- the certificate of design compliance`

#ASSERT `Where does my certificate of design compliance come from` `a certified application` EQUALS `I attach it, signed by a building surveyor, with the plans it specifies`
#ASSERT `Where does my certificate of design compliance come from` `an uncertified application` EQUALS `the permit authority refers my plans to a building surveyor, who decides whether to sign it`

§ `ss 4, 20 -- independence, and must the permit be granted`

#ASSERT `Is my building surveyor independent` `an independent private building surveyor`
-- s 4(2)(b): an employee of the proposed builder is not independent.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my building surveyor independent` `a building surveyor employed by the builder`
-- c055: on the assumed facts the permit authority must grant the permit.
#ASSERT `Must my building permit be granted` `c055: Chloe and Liam's certified application`
-- s 20(1)(d)(ii).
#ASSERT NOT `Must my building permit be granted` `c055 variant: the certificate signed by the builder's own surveyor`
-- s 20(1)(i).
#ASSERT NOT `Must my building permit be granted` `c055 variant: no home indemnity insurance where it is required`

§ `ss 23, 24, 119 -- the decision`

-- No decision, 25-day period (an input) passed.
#ASSERT `Is my application taken to be refused` 30 25 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my application taken to be refused` 20 25 FALSE
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I be told why I was refused` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `May I ask the Tribunal to review` TRUE

§ `s 32 -- duration`

-- No period stated on the permit: 2 years.
#ASSERT `For how many years does my building permit last` 0 EQUALS 2

§ `ss 33, 37 -- completion`

-- c055: the builder gives notice within 7 days of completion.
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I give the notice of completion` `the builder named on Chloe's permit` EQUALS 7
-- c055: not Chloe's duty -- she is not the named builder.
#ASSERT `Within how many days must I give the notice of completion` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` EQUALS 0
-- c055: with a permit, s 37(1) puts it on the builder.
#ASSERT NOT `Must I ensure the finished house meets the building standards` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` `c055: the new Byford house, built under a building permit`
-- s 37(2): built without a permit, it falls on each owner.
#ASSERT `Must I ensure the finished house meets the building standards` `Chloe, a registered proprietor of the Byford lot` `the Byford house built with no permit`

§ `s 41, s 66(5) -- the occupancy permit`

-- c055: only if the regulations under s 66(5) exempt the house; the Act itself does not.
#ASSERT NOT `Must the house have an occupancy permit` `c055: the Byford house at handover, if the regulations exempt it, no occupancy permit`
-- c055 variant: if the regulations do not exempt it, s 41 requires one.
#ASSERT `Must the house have an occupancy permit` `c055 variant: the Byford house at handover, not exempt, no occupancy permit`
-- c055: Chloe and Liam may move in at handover if the house is exempt.
#ASSERT `May we move in` `c055: the Byford house at handover, if the regulations exempt it, no occupancy permit`
#ASSERT NOT `May we move in` `c055 variant: the Byford house at handover, not exempt, no occupancy permit`
#ASSERT `May we move in` `c055 variant: the Byford house at handover, not exempt, occupancy permit granted`
-- s 41(3).
#ASSERT NOT `May we move in` `an unfinished house, not exempt, no temporary permit`
-- s 40: a tenant is an occupier, bound by s 41 too.
#ASSERT `Would moving in be an offence` `a tenant renting the house` TRUE `c055 variant: the Byford house at handover, not exempt, no occupancy permit`

§ `s 54 -- the occupancy permit application`

#ASSERT `Which certificate must accompany my occupancy permit application` `for a completed building (s 46)` EQUALS `a certificate of construction compliance`

§ `s 133 -- time limits`

-- s 133(3): 6 years.
#ASSERT `Can I still be prosecuted` `building without a building permit (s 9)` 5
-- s 133(4): 3 years -- s 41 is not in the 6-year list.
#ASSERT NOT `Can I still be prosecuted` `occupying without an occupancy permit (s 41)` 4
